{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>Most holy.</b> Holy like one of the holy things." "<b>Whatever touches the altar shall become holy.</b> Like \"whatever touches its flesh shall become holy\" (Leviticus 6:20). Some say it speaks only of the bread — that they may not touch it unless they are consecrated; and the meaning is that they not be impure."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:11.343990997Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}